# Optional extra broadband sources for LOPNOR, named on the deck line after the WPS sub-model.
# Pipistrel fly-over case.  Updated 28-09-2026: every parameter the blade geometry determines is
# taken from it; the rest is either a labelled calibration or switched off.
#
# --- Turbulence-ingestion (Amiet 1975 LE) noise ------------------------------------------------
# NOT geometric.  u' and Lambda are FITTED to the averaged fly-over broadband floor
# (100 Hz - 2 kHz, rms 2.8 dB).  No inflow data exist for this flight and only the averaged
# spectrum is available, so this could not be tested blind: treat the TIN level as a calibration.
tin 1
tin_urms 2.48        # rms upwash [m/s]          (fitted)
tin_lambda 0.1       # integral length scale [m] (fitted)
#
# --- BPM tip-vortex formation noise ------------------------------------------------------------
# Tip shape FROM GEOMETRY (bladeGeom.txt): chord/R is still 0.069 at r/R = 0.975 and extrapolates
# to about 0.058 at the tip, i.e. ~41 % of the maximum chord -> finite, cut ('flat') tip.
# Caveat: the table ends at r/R = 0.975, so rounding in the last 2.5 % of radius would not show.
# alpha_tip is taken automatically from BladeAeroData_HansonFD.txt.
tip 1
tip_shape flat
#
# --- BPM trailing-edge bluntness ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Cannot be taken from the geometry: in every Profiles/Cp_Airfoil_rR*.txt contour the lower
# surface stops 5-9 % chord before the trailing edge ('blunt_h auto' rejects all 29 stations).
# Needs the real trailing-edge thickness or full coordinates near the TE.
blunt 0
blunt_h 0.0          # [m] or 'auto'
blunt_psi 14         # [deg], used only with a fixed blunt_h
